    "questionNumber": "POP Q8",
    "originalQuestionNumber": 8,
    "questionText": "Explain the three dimensions of the F-PEC scale in family business.",
    "questionType": "written_structured",
    "marks": 20,
    "totalMarks": 20,
    "suppliedAnswer": "F-PEC stands for Family Influence through Power, Experience and Culture. Power assesses how far the family controls the enterprise through voting ownership, managerial positions and governance. Experience captures the accumulated involvement of family members and generations, including business knowledge and years of participation. Culture examines how strongly the family's values, assumptions, identity and commitments influence organisational conduct. The scale therefore measures degrees of influence. An enterprise can have strong family power yet comparatively weak culture, or deep inherited experience with outside managers handling operations. Using all three dimensions gives a more complete account than ownership share alone. Quick Revision F-PEC: Power, Experience and Culture; family control; accumulated family knowledge; shared organisational values. -- 9 of 33 -- PSALMDATA PSALMDATA - TELECOM AND COMPUTER CAFE Motto: I CAN DO ALL THINGS Website: http://psalmedu.com Contacts: 09163490176; 09011055579",
