    "originalQuestionNumber": 9,
    "questionText": "Discuss four major components of family involvement.",
    "questionType": "written_structured",
    "marks": 20,
    "totalMarks": 20,
    "suppliedAnswer": "The four components are ownership, management, governance and succession. Ownership concerns family voting rights and the ability to influence important company decisions. Management involves family members who actually organise staff, capital and business operations. Governance refers to the board, family institutions and other structures which direct the firm and monitor decision-making. Succession concerns how authority, knowledge and often ownership transfer between generations. A family may be strongly involved in one component and much less in another; that is why family enterprises have different patterns of control. The components also help identify where a disagreement truly lies - between shareholders, directors, managers or prospective successors. PAST QUESTION - 2025_2 Q4; 2019_2 Q4(a)",
