    "questionText": "Explain the family involvement components and the meaning of familiness.",
    "questionType": "written_structured",
    "marks": 20,
    "totalMarks": 20,
    "suppliedAnswer": "Familiness is the distinctive bundle of resources and capabilities produced when the family, individual members and enterprise interact. It may include unusually strong trust, patient financing, shared history, informal communication, tacit know-how and close networks. Family involvement is seen through ownership, governance, management and succession. In the course's explanation, familiness is a potential competitive advantage only when those unique family-based resources produce useful business outcomes. Time, closure, interdependence and interaction help create this potential. A close family relationship by itself is not sufficient where poor decisions, nepotism or unresolved conflict waste those resources. -- 10 of 33 -- PSALMDATA PSALMDATA - TELECOM AND COMPUTER CAFE Motto: I CAN DO ALL THINGS Website: http://psalmedu.com Contacts: 09163490176; 09011055579",
