    "originalQuestionNumber": 13,
    "questionText": "Distinguish Agency Theory from Stewardship Theory.",
    "questionType": "written_structured",
    "marks": 20,
    "totalMarks": 20,
    "suppliedAnswer": "Agency Theory focuses on the risk that managers acting for owners will pursue different interests or withhold information, creating monitoring and control costs. When family ownership and management coincide, some owner-manager conflicts may reduce, but other conflicts among owners may remain. Stewardship Theory focuses on responsibility, trust and intrinsic motivation. It holds that managers or family members can act as custodians of the enterprise, protecting its long-term welfare even without constant external rewards. The contrast is therefore between guarding against self-serving agency behaviour and enabling committed stewardship. Family enterprises need good governance whichever tendency is more evident. Quick Revision Principal; agent; monitoring costs; aligned interests; owner-manager relationships. TOPIC 4: Stewardship Theory 3.1 Stewardship Theory Stewardship theory contrasts with the narrow self-interest assumptions of agency theory. Here the individual entrusted with a business is motivated by responsibility, achievement, trust, commitment and the longer-term welfare of the enterprise. A family member may treat the company as an extension of family identity and therefore work to preserve it for future generations. The stewardship perspective helps explain patient investment, loyalty and willingness to sacrifice immediate personal rewards. It must still be matched with sound judgement and competence. Commitment to the family business is valuable when it improves decisions, not when it shields poor performance from correction. Stewardship is closely associated with viewing ownership as responsibility for an organisation that should outlast the current generation. A founder may reinvest profits, maintain product quality and protect employees because those actions sustain the enterprise that future relatives will inherit. The same concern can motivate a successor who takes pride in preserving the family name. Where the enterprise needs major change, genuine stewardship means protecting its long-term wellbeing rather than insisting on every traditional practice. Responsibility and good judgement should remain connected. -- 13 of 33 -- PSALMDATA PSALMDATA - TELECOM AND COMPUTER CAFE Motto: I CAN DO ALL THINGS Website: http://psalmedu.com Contacts: 09163490176; 09011055579",
