    "questionText": "Explain why shared family vision and business vision matter.",
    "questionType": "written_structured",
    "marks": 20,
    "totalMarks": 20,
    "suppliedAnswer": "Business vision identifies the enterprise's desired future position in its markets, scale, finances, reputation, employment and profitability. Family vision clarifies what family members intend to contribute, how they view stewardship and whether they agree on reinvestment, dividend payments and continued control. When both are discussed openly, potential disagreements can be addressed before they disrupt operations. A long-term shared vision can encourage patient investment and continuity. A family should preserve useful inherited strengths while allowing each new generation to contribute ideas and adapt strategy to competition. An enterprise without agreed family and business vision may become paralysed by conflicting expectations. Quick Revision Business vision; family vision; reinvestment; stewardship; continuity; cross-generation dialogue. -- 20 of 33 -- PSALMDATA PSALMDATA - TELECOM AND COMPUTER CAFE Motto: I CAN DO ALL THINGS Website: http://psalmedu.com Contacts: 09163490176; 09011055579",
