    "suppliedAnswer": "The material identifies four sets of goals. Economic goals are concerned with creating wealth and preserving the family's financial base. Social goals concern reputation and responsibilities to employees, communities and the nation. Psychological goals are about developing family members' talents, their opportunities and emotional wellbeing. Spiritual goals concern religious commitments, service or a deeper meaning beyond commercial gain. These aims can support one another but may also compete. For example, paying higher immediate dividends may conflict with reinvesting for future growth or with maintaining employment. Families need to discuss their priorities openly to reduce conflict. Quick Revision Four stages: wonder, blunder, thunder, sunder/plunder. Four goals: economic, social, psychological, spiritual. -- 22 of 33 -- PSALMDATA PSALMDATA - TELECOM AND COMPUTER CAFE Motto: I CAN DO ALL THINGS Website: http://psalmedu.com Contacts: 09163490176; 09011055579",
