    "questionNumber": "POP Q25",
    "originalQuestionNumber": 25,
    "questionText": "Discuss five challenges of family businesses.",
    "questionType": "written_structured",
    "marks": 20,
    "totalMarks": 20,
    "suppliedAnswer": "Five challenges supported by the material are: (1) generational transfer and the difficulty of preparing future leaders; (2) conflict arising from differences over jobs, remuneration, control and recognition; (3) nepotism or appointments not based on competence; (4) difficulty attracting and retaining skilled non-family managers; and (5) balancing the business's need for capital and competitive adaptation with the varied financial and personal expectations of relatives. The course also stresses poor planning of business transfers and the need for entrepreneurship training. These challenges can weaken even a historically successful enterprise if its owners rely solely on family loyalty. Quick Revision Transfer planning; skilled workforce; founder centrality; altruism; governance and professionalisation. TOPIC 8: Ownership and Management of Family Business 3.1 Ownership and Management of Family Business Ownership concerns rights and responsibilities connected with the enterprise's assets and voting power. Management concerns the everyday organisation of resources, people and operations. Governance links those areas through strategic decisions, oversight and accountability. Owners must not assume that inheritance of shares automatically gives the ability to operate the firm well. The course notes that family shareholders not active in management can obstruct decisions if they fail to understand the time and financing needs of new investments. Healthy family management requires flexibility, expertise and sound working relationships. Participative leadership can help family and non-family employees contribute, while appointed managers must be held to clear performance standards. -- 23 of 33 -- PSALMDATA PSALMDATA - TELECOM AND COMPUTER CAFE Motto: I CAN DO ALL THINGS Website: http://psalmedu.com Contacts: 09163490176; 09011055579",
