    "questionText": "Define corporate governance, directing and controlling.",
    "questionType": "written_structured",
    "marks": 20,
    "totalMarks": 20,
    "suppliedAnswer": "Corporate governance is the system of structures and processes by which a company is directed, controlled and held accountable. In a family firm it involves family institutions, the board and top management. Directing concerns strategic decisions that shape the future of the enterprise rather than the daily performance of routine work. Controlling means supervising management's progress, checking achievements against objectives and responding when performance departs from expectations. These functions have different purposes: the governing body sets direction and ensures accountability, while managers organise the enterprise's continuing operations. PAST QUESTION - 2019_1 Q4(b); 2023_1 Q4(b)",
    "modelAnswer": "Corporate governance is the system of structures and processes by which a company is directed, controlled and held accountable. In a family firm it involves family institutions, the board and top management. Directing concerns strategic decisions that shape the future of the enterprise rather than the daily performance of routine work. Controlling means supervising management's progress, checking achievements against objectives and responding when performance departs from expectations. These functions have different purposes: the governing body sets direction and ensures accountability, while managers organise the enterprise's continuing operations. PAST QUESTION - 2019_1 Q4(b); 2023_1 Q4(b)",
