    "questionText": "Discuss the role of women in family businesses.",
    "questionType": "written_structured",
    "marks": 20,
    "totalMarks": 20,
    "suppliedAnswer": "The material recognises that women participate in family firms as owners, founders, successors, managers and employees. Some inherited or entered such businesses through marriage, while increasing numbers take control or establish ventures themselves. It also warns that women's abilities may be ignored when they are assigned only nurturing or peacekeeping functions. A family enterprise should assess a member's contribution by competence, interests and actual performance rather than by assumptions about gender. Good governance makes room for fair participation and responsibility across family members. Supporting women's involvement adds capacity to the enterprise and can strengthen long-term continuity. -- 27 of 33 -- PSALMDATA PSALMDATA - TELECOM AND COMPUTER CAFE Motto: I CAN DO ALL THINGS Website: http://psalmedu.com Contacts: 09163490176; 09011055579",
