    "questionText": "Why is weak succession planning a major cause of failure in family-controlled businesses?",
    "questionType": "written_structured",
    "marks": 20,
    "totalMarks": 20,
    "suppliedAnswer": "Succession is more than replacing a founder's name on an office door. It can change who owns shares, who directs the company, who manages daily operations and how other family members are treated. Without preparation, an unwilling or unqualified heir may take charge, shareholders may disagree, trusted employees may leave and the company may lose strategic direction. Legal, tax and financing obligations can add pressure. The course therefore treats succession as a gradual process: develop successors, plan ownership transition, agree governance roles, build trust, consult the family and preserve valuable business capabilities while allowing new leadership to adapt. -- 28 of 33 -- PSALMDATA PSALMDATA - TELECOM AND COMPUTER CAFE Motto: I CAN DO ALL THINGS Website: http://psalmedu.com Contacts: 09163490176; 09011055579",
