    "questionText": "Explain the three patterns of ineffective succession.",
    "questionType": "written_structured",
    "marks": 20,
    "totalMarks": 20,
    "suppliedAnswer": "Conservative succession occurs when the new leader remains under the shadow of the previous generation and is unable to adapt inherited strategies. Rebellious succession occurs when the new generation rejects the past too strongly, discarding useful tradition, knowledge or even the core business model. Wavering succession occurs when successors are indecisive: they do not renew the business but also fail to provide clear, stable leadership. These patterns share a lack of balanced judgement. A successful successor should learn from earlier achievement, independently evaluate current challenges and make suitable changes with the support of employees, advisers and relatives. Quick Revision Conservative; rebellious; wavering succession. -- 29 of 33 -- PSALMDATA PSALMDATA - TELECOM AND COMPUTER CAFE Motto: I CAN DO ALL THINGS Website: http://psalmedu.com Contacts: 09163490176; 09011055579",
