    "questionText": "Explain five common mistakes of succession in a family business.",
    "questionType": "written_structured",
    "marks": 20,
    "totalMarks": 20,
    "suppliedAnswer": "Five major mistakes are: (1) confusing ownership, governance and management, so an heir is assumed to be fit for every role; (2) treating family succession as an obligation to preserve the past, irrespective of the child's interest; (3) treating succession as one event rather than a long learning and handover process; (4) failing to transmit entrepreneurial initiative, confidence and willingness to respond to change; and (5) failing to sustain constructive dialogue between parents and children. The course also identifies two further mistakes: relying on inherited values without adapting them to new circumstances and selecting an unsuitable external adviser or third actor. The common solution is merit, preparation and open discussion. -- 30 of 33 -- PSALMDATA PSALMDATA - TELECOM AND COMPUTER CAFE Motto: I CAN DO ALL THINGS Website: http://psalmedu.com Contacts: 09163490176; 09011055579",
