    "questionText": "Discuss four ways to avoid mistakes of succession in family business.",
    "questionType": "written_structured",
    "marks": 20,
    "totalMarks": 20,
    "suppliedAnswer": "First, adopt a proper concept of ownership: family shares bring responsibility to the enterprise, workers, financiers and community, not an unrestricted licence to use business resources personally. Second, develop a culture of merit: future leaders should be assessed by real ability, experience and results, and relatives who lack the right competencies should be supported into suitable alternatives. Third, educate the young: transfer skills and values through personal example, explanation, mentoring and practical experience. Fourth, choose a deliberate entrepreneurial development model so that later generations acquire initiative, informed risk-taking and an ability to create value. These safeguards make transition a prepared process rather than an inheritance-based gamble. Quick Revision Responsible ownership; merit; educating heirs; entrepreneurial development; fair assessment. -- 31 of 33 -- PSALMDATA PSALMDATA - TELECOM AND COMPUTER CAFE Motto: I CAN DO ALL THINGS Website: http://psalmedu.com Contacts: 09163490176; 09011055579",
