    "questionText": "List and describe characteristics of successful successors.",
    "questionType": "written_structured",
    "marks": 20,
    "totalMarks": 20,
    "suppliedAnswer": "Successful successors: (1) understand and care about the business; (2) know their own strengths and weaknesses through suitable education and outside experience; (3) genuinely wish to lead and serve; (4) accept responsible mentoring from the previous generation, advisers and directors; (5) maintain good working relations with relatives and colleagues; (6) draw on competent non-family managers to complement their skills; (7) have sufficient controlling influence or trusted allies; (8) earn the respect of employees, customers, suppliers and family members; (9) possess abilities that match the firm's strategic needs; and (10) honour the past while focusing effort on the future. These qualities explain why appointment by birth order alone is not a reliable succession plan. Quick Revision Business knowledge; self-knowledge; service; mentoring; relationships; expert support; legitimacy; fit; respect; future focus. -- 33 of 33 --",
